# CVE-2026-47884 (spring-webmvc XsltView path / RCE).
# This project does not use XsltView or view-name rendering from "/**" mappings;
# it only exposes a JSON SSE endpoint. The OSS fix is Spring Framework 7.0.9
# (Spring Boot 4.0.8+). The 6.2.20 patch is enterprise-only and is not on
# Maven Central, so Boot 3.5.x cannot clear the finding by a patch bump.
# Revisit when upgrading to Spring Boot 4.x.
CVE-2026-47884

# CVE-2026-47890 (Spring Framework: SSE stream corruption when pushing view fragments).
# Affected: spring-webmvc / spring-webflux 6.2.0-6.2.19 and 7.0.0-7.0.8; fixed in 7.0.9.
# Checked 2026-10-13: 6.2.20 is not published on Maven Central (HTTP 404), so Boot 3.5.x has no
# open-source patch to bump to.
# The affected branch runs only when the SSE payload is a ModelAndView
# (DefaultSseEmitterHandler -> FragmentHandler.handle), read from the 6.2.19 bytecode in use.
# This project pushes SseEmitter event builders carrying JSON strings and declares no view
# resolver, template engine, or fragment rendering, so the branch is never entered.
# Host applications that do stream view fragments over SSE need Spring Boot 4 / Framework 7.0.9.
# Revisit when upgrading to Spring Boot 4.x.
CVE-2026-47890
